h-mad/SKILL.md:3189:- `h_mad_delta_stage.py` — stages the ADVISORY `doc-auditor` delta review per phase (§"Delta self-review"): CLI (`--feature F --project-root ROOT --sha SHA --phase P … --answers REPORT …`) printing `DELTA-STAGE: STAGED phase=<p> report=<path> prompt=<path>` plus the exact `Agent(subagent_type: "doc-auditor", …)` call per phase, exit 0; `DELTA-STAGE: HALT <what>:<reason>` and exit 3 on any refusal (`sha:unresolvable|not_a_commit`, `<phase>:doc_missing|unchanged|git_error|name_in_audit_grammar|report_path_handed`, `answers:missing|not_a_file|empty|unreadable`, `<arg>:control_char` for a control character in any value the prompt interpolates, `prompt:unwritable` — the last after removing this run's own prompts and claims), with nothing claimed and nothing written; exit 2 on a usage error, including a `--feature` outside `[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*`. Every check runs before the first claim, and an unevaluable check halts. **It mints the report name and has no flag to override it** — `<feature>.<phase>.delta-review.<sha7>-<UTC stamp>.md`, never `vN` — and refuses a name that `h_mad_cycle_counts._VERSION_RE`, `h_mad_audit_gate._STAMP_NAME_RE` or a `.audit.` segment would select, reading those regexes from their modules at call time so the check tracks the grammar. Resolves each phase's document through the assembler's `doc_path()`, and claims the report and prompt paths once through the assembler's claim-once markers (`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/h-mad/handed`), releasing only its own fresh claims when a later phase's claim is refused. It stages; the `Agent()` dispatch stays the orchestrator's. Stdlib-only.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3190:- `h_mad_audit_origins.py` — per-must origin tagging (#11/H7): `validate()` / `read_sidecar()` / `aggregate()` / `share()` + two subcommands. `append` validates one must-fix record and appends it to `<docs-root>/03-analysis/<feature>.audit-origins.jsonl` (or `--sidecar`), printing `ORIGINS: APPENDED cycle=N origin=X leg=L`; an invalid record is REFUSED and nothing is written, since a malformed record on disk is counted by every later summary. `summary` prints one `ORIGINS: OK|INVALID|UNREADABLE n=N accepted=A rejected=R fix-introduced=C/A (P%) self-caught=C/A (P%) cycles=lo-hi` line, an origins breakdown, then the `[H-MAD]` marker; `--per-cycle` gives the trend the hypothesis is about and `--cell` prints ledger table cells for the owning lane to paste. Exit 0 on a verdict, 1 on `INVALID`, 2 on a cannot-judge. **The eight origins are the ledger's** and an unknown one is the single hard error over content — a typo that becomes its own bucket lowers `fix-introduced` and reads as the loop improving. `by_cycle` is required for `fix-introduced`/`propagation-gap` only; other origins may carry it (33 of the prototype's 152 do) and unknown keys pass through, because `severity`/`note` are in the real corpus and were never in the schema block. An **absent sidecar is `UNREADABLE`, never a rate of zero**, and an unparsable line is named with its line number rather than skipped — both are the same failure family, an absence that spells like a good result. The fix-introduced denominator excludes `rejected` and the output says so. Calibrated against the 152-record `gateway-consolidation` prototype (cycles 98–103) copied to `tests/fixtures/`: every hard rule fires zero times on it. Stdlib-only.
