h-mad/SKILL.md:3192:- `h_mad_audit_gate.py` — audit-gate verdict unit (single source of truth): `classify()` (three keys, every caller) / `classify_detail()` (plus the per-class breakdown) + CLI printing `GATE: PASS|FAIL must=N should=N`, then `GATE-CLASS: build=N measurement=M untagged=K ack_refused=R` (§"Finding class — build vs measurement": untagged and unknown count as build; a `class: build` bullet is refused by the sidecar), then, on a stamped PASS, `GATE-LEGS: <a>+<b>|unrecorded` (§"Name the reviewer legs"; `--legs NAME` repeatable, normalised sorted/deduped into the stamp as `legs`, `null` when unnamed — never `[]`, which would claim zero legs ran), then the `[H-MAD]` marker. **Full emission order is four lines, and `SUITE:` comes FIRST** — `SUITE:` → `GATE:` → `GATE-CLASS:` → `GATE-LEGS:` — measured by executing the CLI on 2026-09-07 (`docs/03-analysis/hmad-gate-field-verification.md`); an earlier revision of this entry described three lines starting at `GATE:`. Nothing anchors on the order (`GATE_RE` matches by line), but a documented sequence that omits a line is a claim that does not survive execution. `SUITE:` is absent without `--project-tests` and `GATE-LEGS:` without `--gated`, exit 0 on verdict / 2 on operational error; `--must-only` for the `/h-mad do` precondition. `--exit-check <stamp>…` prints `EXIT: READY|BLOCKED|UNREADABLE`, refusing a streak whose suite was red or unmeasured (#91) or whose **leg set changed between the two cycles** (#11/H3, `reason=legs_changed:<a>|<b>`); an unrecorded leg set is reported as `legs=unrecorded`, never blocked. Imported by `h_mad_do_preconditions.py` Since #15 an `## Acknowledged-not-fixed` bullet matches a finding through canonicalisation (emphasis, backticks, wrapping, case, trailing punctuation) or an explicit leading `[key]`; **never through text similarity** — see §"Why the ack match is not fuzzy" for the measurement that refused it.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3193:- `h_mad_doc_consumers.py` — **which tests parse the document I am about to commit?** `consumers()` + CLI (`[--staged] [--run] [PATH …]`) printing `CONSUMERS: <doc> n=K` and the test files, then one `RUN: python3 -m pytest -q …` line; `CONSUMERS: UNKNOWN` when git cannot answer; exit 0 always without `--run`. A doc-derived test lives beside its consumer, never beside the document, so a targeted slice misses it. Before committing a document edit, run `h_mad_doc_consumers.py <repo-relative doc> --run` rather than copying the `RUN:` line into a shell: it executes that line's own file list with the interpreter running the script (`sys.executable`, named on a `RUN-WITH:` line; through the shebang that is the `python3` on PATH, so a pytest-less one is refused, not spawned), streams pytest's output to stderr, and ends with `CONSUMERS-RUN: PASS files=K passed=N` (exit 0), `FAIL files=K failed=N` plus the FAILED ids (exit 1), `NONE` when nothing reads the documents (exit 0), or `UNREADABLE reason=pytest-missing|no-summary|unknown-docs|timeout|interrupted|incomplete` (exit 2: no pytest; no summary line; no document, a missing one, or an absolute or out-of-repo path, which would name another worktree's copy; `--timeout`, default 1800 s; Ctrl-C; or nothing failed but nothing passed or pytest exited non-zero, with `rc=` and `summary=`). Never PASS on any of these. Read the token. For `h-mad/SKILL.md` it runs ~77 files, several minutes. Wired as the advisory `git-hooks/pre-commit` (installed by `git-hooks/install.sh`), which runs it WITHOUT `--run`, prints the list on stderr and never blocks.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3194:- `h_mad_branch_evidence.py` — **what did that worktree executor actually land?** `collect()` + CLI (`<worktree-or-branch> [--base main] [--no-mutation] [--child-timeout S]`) printing `EVIDENCE: sha=<9> base=<9> ahead=N dirty=N`, the commits, changed files and derived sets, then `TESTS:`, the forwarded `h_mad_doc_consumers.py --run` token `CONSUMERS-RUN:`, the harness's `ANCHORS:` line and one `MUTATION: <spec> <verdict>` per spec over changed code with its `survived:`/`refused:` rows (a spec that only targets a changed document is anchor-checked, not run), strictly in sequence with `sys.executable`; last line `EVIDENCE-VERDICT: COMPLETE [waived=no-mutation]` (exit 0), `INCOMPLETE reason=dirty|no-commits|no-tests|no-mutation-spec|deleted-guard|tests-failed|consumers-failed|anchors-drifted|mutation-<verdict>` (exit 0; `--no-mutation` waives only `no-mutation-spec`) or `UNREADABLE reason=…` (exit 2: pytest missing, crashed, timed out or passing nothing; `suite-busy` or `suite-tree-moved` from the suite lock; a child with no token or a BUSY/UNREADABLE/TREE_MOVED/RESTORE_FAILED one; `interrupted`; an unknown base or a directory that is not a worktree's top; `tree-moved` when HEAD or the status changed during the run). It never writes into the worktree it measures: a child that times out or is interrupted gets SIGTERM, so the harness restores its mutant, then SIGKILL for its whole process group.
h-mad/SKILL.md:3195:- `h_mad_ac_census.py` — re-derives a spec's AC count and checks paired docs: `parse()` / `numbering_findings()` / `claim_findings()` + CLI (`<spec> [<paired doc> …]`) printing `ACS: OK|DRIFT count=N frs=K`, `ACS: NONE count=0` or `ACS: UNREADABLE`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 unreadable. DRIFT = an `All N ACs` claim that disagrees, a numbering gap or duplicate, or a lettered AC without its base. Document order is `ORDER (advisory):` only: calibrated on the committed corpus, four audited specs place ACs by topic and none has a gap, and the one DRIFT it reports there is real (`fanout-integrity-and-defects.plan.md` says 34, the spec has 35).
