3181:- `h_mad_collect_report.py` — collect-report surface collector: copies a delivered report-file or `--out` fallback into the docs audit path (the fallback reads a pane scrape past the dispatch boundary and an `exec` `--out` file from its end — see §6.6; conflating the two made it dead for `exec`), prints `COLLECT: OK|MISSING|CONFLICT` plus the collected path/delivery source, and performs readback before reporting success. `OK`/`MISSING`/`CONFLICT` exit 0 because they are measured outcomes; operational errors and readback failures exit 2. `--force` overwrites an existing collected report after a conflict.
3268:- `h_mad_review_evidence.py` — 6a-prime evidence gate: `scan()` + CLI printing `EVIDENCE: PASS|NONE tools=N ok=K failed=J thinking=T [status=…]`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 on `EVIDENCE: UNREADABLE reason=no_log|empty_log|unsupported_format`, which carries **no counts** so a cannot-judge cannot read as a zero. Answers only "did the review read anything" — never whether its findings are right. Counts any tool reaching `DONE`, knows no tool names, and reports `result.status` without gating on it. `thinking=` sums `usage.thinking_tokens` over completed `agent_response` steps and is reported for the same reason `status` is — triage, never a verdict (J49). With `--project-root <root>` the line (and the codex `CODEXEVIDENCE:` and grok lines) ends with `paths=N code=C other=O unmeasured=U`: the distinct EXISTING paths the calls named, split into code (under the root, outside its docs/ tree) and other (docs/ or outside the root), and the calls whose targets the transcript does not show (codex MCP calls print no arguments). Without a root the fields are absent, never zero, and they never change a verdict or an exit code. The audit-cycle driver threads its own root through, shows the same fields beside `tools=` in the `Effort:` block, records them in each pass's `.effort.json` sidecar, and copies the pass log to the project's `.h-mad/pass-logs/` directory under the collected report's name with its `log_sha256` (a failed copy records `log_retained: null` and a reason, and never costs the verdict). That directory writes its own `*` ignore file, and it is never pruned: each pass adds a full transcript (calibration logs ran 7–386 KB), so clear it by hand, for example at feature archive. Read `code=` as a floor: `other=` also carries the pass's own report file and its `.done` marker, and a `cd` inside one command line or a path quoted inside an inline `-c` script is not followed, so those calls read as zero targets rather than `unmeasured`. Stdlib-only.
